  "description": "Retries of reads. delay: attempt is 0-based (the delay before the 2nd call is attempt 0); without retry_after the delay is min(cap, base * 2^attempt) times a uniform random factor in [0.5, 1): expected.min is the factor 0.5, expected.max the exclusive upper bound; with a finite retry_after (seconds) it is max(0, min(cap, retry_after)) with no jitter (min = max); a non-finite retry_after (the strings NaN / Infinity in input) is ignored and the backoff applies. should_retry: true only for a read (state_changing false) whose error is NetworkError, RequestTimeoutError, RateLimitError or ServerError, while attempt < max_retries. retry_after_header: a finite numeric Retry-After header (seconds, sign kept) on an HTTP 429 RateLimitError sets retry_after; anything else (an HTTP date, nan, inf, another status) leaves null.",
  "source": "tradesmart._transport.retry.RetryPolicy / tradesmart._transport.sync_http.apply_retry_after",
  "tolerance": {
    "abs": 1e-12
  }
}
